<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!-- Wide fascias - the 1280x720 console this car has, and anything above 1000dp of width.

         The equaliser row here has room to spare once the subwoofer frequency dropdown is down to
         the width of "100 Hz" plus its arrow, so the five buttons of that row (amplifier volume
         minus/plus and the quick actions minus/plus/zero) are 68dp rather than the 48dp base. They
         are meant to be hit without looking, by a driver, in a moving car; the base value exists
         for narrow windows, not as the target to aim for.

         Measured on the unit 12.09.2026: at 36dp the row was uniform and unusable. -->
    <dimen name="eq_action_button">68dp</dimen>

    <!-- Same reasoning for the subwoofer slider: this panel has the room, so the thumb is bigger
         still - 13dp of radius is 26dp of target, which is a thumb on a moving car's fascia. -->
    <dimen name="eq_slider_thumb">13dp</dimen>

    <!-- Room enough for "Підсилення:" and "Субвуфер:" in full, so neither is ever shortened here
         and neither is padded out with empty space. -->
    <dimen name="eq_caption_max">170dp</dimen>
</resources>
